    "Orofacial myofunctional therapy (OMT) addresses the muscles of the face, mouth, and tongue, and the habits they've learned. A low-resting tongue, an open-mouth posture, or a persistent thumb-sucking habit might look minor, but these patterns influence how a child sleeps, eats, speaks, and even how their face and airway grow.",
    "Mouth breathing is the classic example. A child who breathes through their mouth often sleeps poorly, and poor sleep can look like ADHD in the classroom. Shallow breathing has a negative impact on the nervous system and can contribute to a state of fight or flight. And the cycle compounds. This airway-sensory connection is the heart of Dr. Marielly's Therastacking approach, and it's why families are referred to us by dentists, orthodontists, and ENTs across Los Angeles and beyond.",
    "Therapy is a structured program of playful, age-appropriate exercises that retrain breathing, tongue posture, chewing, and swallowing, often in coordination with your child's dentist, ENT, or orthodontist.",
